{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1440635-creatures-of-the-gauntlet","id":1440635,"title":"Creatures of the Gauntlet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-19T14:33:02-07:00","id":1440635,"title":"Creatures of the Gauntlet","content":"So on page 151 of Shunned by the Moon it talks about creatures living in the gauntlet, it mentions invasive speeches that have wormed their way(including some hosts) but it also mentions True residents of the Gauntlet. So I am wondering what kind of creatures could you imagine living in the Gauntlet..ignoring Idigam, Hosts, and Geryo that is. I might homebrew something but I wondered if the more lore-wise WTF players could come with their input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T14:49:11-07:00","id":1440640,"title":"","content":"Summoners, for Mage: the Awakening First Edition, touches on the subject, but to paint a fairly dull picture, at least from the perspective of mages. Using their sorcery to peer between the &quot;layers of the Gauntlet,&quot; they glimpse a misty nowhere-land, and the ephemeral beings they've documented are small, fragile, animalistic creatures, somewhat like the spirit equivalent of what bacteria and protozoa are to plant and animal life, which die when summoned out of the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Not posting to limit brainstorming and ideas; I think we could do with something a little more gameable than that. You could probably even keep the spirit-protozoans if you suppose that the phrase &quot;layers of the Gauntlet&quot; suggests the spell being used to glimpse them is zooming in on a level too fine, and more complicated phenomena are, so to speak, multifoliate, taking shape <i>across</i> whatever these &quot;layers&quot; would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-19-2021, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T15:32:39-07:00","id":1440649,"title":"","content":"First edition was working off of some things that have changed in second edition.<br /> <br /> Now, basically anything that was in Pangaea when the Sundering occurred could be living there. This includes clans of humans, werewolves, and other supernaturals that were living there or otherwise got herded there by other forces. While the Sundering Dark Era doesn't get into it much as a land of predators and prey I ran Pangaea with a lot of fauna that fit that cycle. Long serpents with eyes down their sides, rabbits with legs as big as their trunk that could run at ridiculous speeds and hop incredibly high, packs of wolves that had camouflage that made them basically translucent like the Predator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T12:10:33-07:00","id":1441537,"title":"","content":"Hmm... my response got et. I had a few ideas to play with:<br /> <br /> Pillars: Stone spirits or pangeans with specific natures focusing on resistance to change, stability, and the like. The have an effect, whether through arcana or numin, that maintains an area around them where the Gauntlet never formed, but rather functions as Pangea, still. <br /> <br /> Shades: Ephemera that can slip through corners, which is how they access the Gauntlet. They tend to feast on ephemeral essences and can usually manipulate some specific form of immaterial state that is more generally phrased as a lack of some trait such as shadow or fear. This specialty of theirs can be manipulated to shape and otherwise behave in odd ways for longer than a spirit can usually maintain such an effect. Those that focus on ectoplasm sometimes consume enough ghost essences to become ghostlike, developing the appearance and powers of ghosts.<br /> <br /> Ygg: Tree pangea that send out branches or shoots into other realms. These operate as spirits of shadow, almost exclusively., but in the material realm, they tend to possess trees that are similar enough to be open. If enough shoots remain connected, the Ygg cannot ever die, though an Ygg can be fragmented into shartha by destroying the pangean form. Once that happens, the shoots and branches are treated as independent spirits..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}